         "1. Initial state: solid fragrant paste coated on a thin bamboo splinter.\n2. Combustion: burning tip glows red, consuming organic binders and perfume oils.\n3. Production of new substances: fine grey mineral ash drops onto the stand; smoke carries carbon dioxide and aromatic gases throughout the room.\n4. Permanence: stick length shortens to zero; ash has no structural cohesion or combustible fuel.\n5. Conclude: formation of ash, smoke, and heat is definitive evidence of an irreversible chemical change.",
