         "1. Fuel: liquified petroleum gas (predominantly butane C4H10).\n2. Spark & combustion: 2C4H10 + 13O2 -> 8CO2 + 10H2O + intense heat and light energy.\n3. Dispersal: invisible CO2 and water vapour escape through the kitchen exhaust fan.\n4. Reversibility test: cooling the kitchen air does not condense LPG fuel back into the gas pipe.\n5. Conclude: combustion of fossil fuels is completely irreversible.",
