         "1. Graph construction: X-axis = Time (minutes: 0, 15, 30, 45, 60); Y-axis = Candle Length (cm: 0 to 12).\n2. Plotting coordinates: (0, 12), (15, 9.5), (30, 7.0), (45, 4.5), (60, 2.0).\n3. Trend analysis: line slopes downwards linearly from top left to bottom right.\n4. Rate of combustion calculation: ΔLength / ΔTime = (12 - 2) / 60 = 10 cm / 60 min = 0.167 cm/min (1 cm every 6 minutes).\n5. Scientific deduction: the steady negative slope proves irreversible mass consumption into gaseous combustion products.\n6. Extrapolation: at 72 minutes, candle length reaches 0 cm (completely burnt out).",
