         "1. Starting material: 20 cm x 20 cm square white paper sheet.\n2. Path A (Folding): folding creases paper along geometric lines -> unfold completely -> flat paper sheet recovered (Reversible physical transformation).\n3. Path B (Cutting): scissors shear cellulose fibres along multiple cut lines -> produces 200 confetti pieces.\n4. Reversibility check Path B: can confetti be reassembled into a single intact sheet without foreign adhesive? No -> Irreversible physical transformation.\n5. Comparative takeaway: mechanical reshaping can be reversible (folding) or irreversible (severing/cutting).\n6. Conclude: physical changes can be either reversible or irreversible.",
